// Arithmetic on a provider output INSIDE a `guardrails { … }` block.
//
// This is the shape the old closed `guardrails { … }` grammar could not
// express: it admitted only a boolean combination of provider atoms with a
// bare comparison, so `count + 1 <= 3` (arithmetic on the output) was a
// parse error inside the block — it worked only in an unwrapped `when { … }`
// (see case 0010). After the provider-path unification a `guardrails { … }`
// block IS a full Cedar expression, so arithmetic, `&&` with a plain Cedar
// condition, etc. all compose here exactly as in a bare `when { … }`.
//
// Same policy as 0010, but wrapped in a `guardrails { … }` block to prove
// the wrapped form now has the unwrapped form's full expressiveness. Permit
// Read when the request is flagged trusted AND the document has at most two
// digits (`digitCount + 1 <= 3`).

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    context.input.trusted == true
    && Strings::DigitCount(context.input.document).count + 1 <= 3
};
